    "name": "flow_divergence_x_spread_z",
    "mechanism": "Stress-gated absorption: the flow_divergence signal (book flow minus trade flow) is strongest when it must EXPLAIN itself against stressed quoting. When spreads are wide (makers fearful, adverse selection high), a book that still builds one side beyond what executed aggression justifies is almost certainly informed stealth flow -> strong continuation at 15-60s. The same divergence under unusually tight, comfortable spreads may be routine queue noise. Multiplying by spread z gates the champion signal by the quoting state; the product is sign-symmetric and near-orthogonal to either parent.",
